+
+/*
+ * The alignment shift of a kernel stack allocation: 32 KiB, so a stack region is always aligned to
+ * 1 << 15 bytes. A 16 KiB-page Apple kernel derives this from the page shift; this port runs a 4 KiB
+ * kernel on the same 32 KiB-aligned allocations, so the number is not PAGE_SHIFT.
+ *
+ * One original component reads it as a page shift for its own bounds check: AppleMobileFileIntegrity
+ * keeps PAGE_SHIFT_CONST in a GOT slot, and its only reader is CoreEntitlements' DER iterator, which
+ * tests sp & ((1 << *slot) - 1) < 0x80 and reports "out of stack" below that. On this kernel a stack
+ * starts 8 KiB into a 32 KiB-aligned region, so the page shift (and 14) makes that test fail at fixed
+ * call depths (OSEntitlements copyDictionary failed with 14 on the exec path). The prelink binds that
+ * one GOT slot to this symbol instead, for which sp & mask stays at least 8 KiB inside any stack; the
+ * other components keep PAGE_SHIFT_CONST for page arithmetic.
+ */
+int unixnu_kernel_stack_shift = 15;
